  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ACT Alliance- Global Programme on Gender Justice 2019-2023</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ACT Alliance- Global programme on Gender Justice 2019-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">By 2023, the expected impact is that ACT Alliance and its members have contributed to changed policy, practice, narratives and attitudes on gender justice in faith-communities, by positively affecting the commitment of churches and other FBOs within the Alliance, as well as their programming and their advocacy efforts to realise gender justice.
To ensure that all members and partners are able to contribute towards this overall goal, the programme is aiming at securing&#xa0; four outcomes, during a four year period:
1. ACT Alliance members are committed to promote changes in policy, practice, attitudes and structural arrangements, towards a more gender just distribution of power
2. The programmatic work contributes to gender just societies
3. ACT Alliance is a global progressive force for gender justice contributing to the SDGs and connecting the dynamics of local-global-local initiatives
4. The programme providers&#x2019; capacity and quality of interventions are enhanced</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen avser ett 44 MSEK-programst&#xf6;d till ACT Alliance: s globala j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsprogram 2019&#x2013;2023, genom strategin f&#xf6;r Sveriges utvecklingssamarbete f&#xf6;r global j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet och kvinnors och flickors r&#xe4;ttigheter 2018&#x2013;2022. Den totala budgeten f&#xf6;r programmet &#xe4;r 4 525 110 USD.

ACT Alliance &#xe4;r en trosbaserad akt&#xf6;r som representerar v&#xe4;rldens st&#xf6;rsta n&#xe4;tverk av protestantiska och ortodoxa kyrkor. ACT Svenska kyrkan &#xe4;r medlem i ACT Alliance och har en aktiv roll i denna insats. Medlemmarna i ACT Alliance &#xe4;r associerade med V&#xe4;rldsr&#xe5;det f&#xf6;r kyrkor eller det Lutherska v&#xe4;rldsf&#xf6;rbundet. Cirka 70% av ACT Alliance-medlemmarna &#xe4;r nationella kyrkor eller trosbaserade kyrkorelaterade organisationer fr&#xe5;n Syd.

ACT Alliance &#xe4;r en nyckelakt&#xf6;r i arbetet f&#xf6;r &#xf6;kad global j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet. De utmanar teologi som motverkar genusr&#xe4;ttvisa och j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet och mobiliserar religi&#xf6;sa ledare f&#xf6;r j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet. Genom att bidra till f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndrade samh&#xe4;llsnormer, policyer och praxis kommer ACT Alliance att spela en viktig roll f&#xf6;r uppn&#xe5;endet av SDG 5 och den &#xf6;vergripande visionen om en j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lld och r&#xe4;ttvis v&#xe4;rld d&#xe4;r m&#xe4;nniskor har makt att fritt forma samh&#xe4;llen, trossamfund och sina egna liv.

&#xc5;r 2023 r&#xe4;knar programmet med att ha bidragit till f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndrade policys, praxis, narrativ och attityder som leder till &#xf6;kad genusr&#xe4;ttvisa och j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet inom trossamfund. Detta genom att uppmuntra och st&#xf6;dja progressiva krafter och engagemang inom alliansen, genom att &#xf6;ka antalet program f&#xf6;r ett transformativt j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsarbete, samt genom p&#xe5;verkansarbete. Detta f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntas uppn&#xe5;s genom att: 
1. Aktivera och mobilisera ACT Alliance-medlemmars &#xe5;taganden f&#xf6;r att fr&#xe4;mja f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringar i attityder och strukturer f&#xf6;r &#xf6;kad genusr&#xe4;ttvisa och j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet. 
2. St&#xf6;dja ACT Alliance nationella samarbetsplattformar (forum) i utformningen och implementeringen av programmatiskt arbete f&#xf6;r &#xf6;kad j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet. 
3. Anv&#xe4;nda sin unika position och n&#xe4;tverk f&#xf6;r att fungera som en global progressiv kraft f&#xf6;r genusr&#xe4;ttvisa och j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet, bidra till de globala utvecklingsm&#xe5;len samt koppla samman arbetet som sker p&#xe5; det nationell, regional och global niv&#xe5;. 
4. St&#xe4;rka alliansmedlemmarnas kapacitet inom j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet b&#xe5;de p&#xe5; individ och institutionell niv&#xe5; f&#xf6;r att s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla &#xf6;kad kvalit&#xe9; p&#xe5; de program som genomf&#xf6;rs.  

Sida bed&#xf6;mer att ACT Alliance som &#xe4;r en trosbaserad akt&#xf6;r med ett omfattande medlemsn&#xe4;tverk och som arbetar med b&#xe5;de humanit&#xe4;rt bist&#xe5;nd, l&#xe5;ngsiktigt utvecklingssamarbete och p&#xe5;verkan, &#xe4;r en relevant samarbetspart till Sida och ser dess kompletterande roll till civilsamh&#xe4;llesakt&#xf6;rer som arbetar f&#xf6;r j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet. Progressiva trosbaserade r&#xf6;relser som syftar till att fr&#xe4;mja en teologi som f&#xf6;respr&#xe5;kar genusr&#xe4;ttvisa och j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;llhet beh&#xf6;ver st&#xf6;d, speciellt p&#xe5; grund av det v&#xe4;xande motst&#xe5;ndet mot j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet bland annat fr&#xe5;n trosbaserade akt&#xf6;rer, samt det krympande utrymmet f&#xf6;r det civila samh&#xe4;llet.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention refers to a 44 MSEK program support to ACT Alliance&apos;s Global Gender Justice Programme 2019-2023, through the Strategy for Sweden&#x2019;s development cooperation for global gender equality and women&#x2019;s and girls&#x2019; rights 2018&#x2013;2022. The total budget for the programme is 4 525 110 USD. 

ACT Alliance is a faith based organization (FBO), representing the world&#xb4;s largest network of Protestant and Orthodox churches and agencies. The ACT Church of Sweden is a member with an active role in this intervention. Overall ACT Alliance&apos;s members are associated with the World Council of Churches or the Lutheran World Federation. Around 70% of ACT Alliance&apos;s members are national churches or faith-based church-related organisations from the Global South. 

ACT Alliance as a faith-based network is in a key position to act in the transformation of gender injustices by bridging the discourse of religion with that of secular and human rights, and by mobilizing faith leaders. By contributing to changed societal norms, policies and practices through this intervention, ACT Alliance will play a part in contributing to the achievement of SDG5, and the overall vision of a world where gender equality and justice are realised as equal enjoyment of human rights, and where people have the power to freely shape societies, faith communities and their own lives.

By 2023, the Programme expects to have contributed to changed policy, practice, narratives and attitudes on gender justice in faith-communities, by positively affecting the commitment of churches and other faith-based organisations within the Alliance, as well as their programming and their advocacy to promote and realise gender justice. This will be achieved by:
1. Enabling and mobilizing ACT Alliance members&#x2019; commitment to promote changes in attitudes and structural arrangements towards a more gender just distribution of power 
2. Supporting ACT Alliance Forums in shaping and implementing programmatic work that contributes to gender just societies 
 3. Using its unique position and networks to act as a global progressive force for gender justice, contributing to the SDGs and connecting the national to the regional and global levels 
4. Ensuring that the programme providers&#x2019; capacity in the programme areas is strengthened, so that the programme providers and their implementing staff are both institutionally and individually more skilled in the area of gender justice.

Sida assesses the network and role of ACT Alliance as a FBO working with development, humanitarian aid and advocating for gender justice as relevant and additional to civil society engaged in transformational work for gender equality. Progressive faith based movements engaged in promoting a positive faith discourse for gender equality need support, especialy in the midst of a growing backlash on gender equality and shrinking space for civil society, including from faith based groups.</narrative>
  </description>
